derivations.claim:
Bracket invariance: for $C^{2}$ functions $f,g$ on $W_{2}$, the chain rule of [F2] gives $
abla(f\circ C)(z)=DC(z)^{\mathsf T}
abla f(C(z))$ and $
abla(g\circ C)(z)=DC(z)^{\mathsf T}
abla g(C(z))$, so $\{f\circ C,g\circ C\}(z)=
abla f(C(z))^{\mathsf T}DC(z)J\,DC(z)^{\mathsf T}
abla g(C(z))=
abla f(C(z))^{\mathsf T}J
abla g(C(z))=\{f,g\}(C(z))$ by step 1.1 and the bracket formula of [F1]; this is clause 2.

